@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Work Items in the Basic Process";
    Layout = "~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLayout.cshtml";
}

@await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureContentStyles.cshtml")

<div class="row g-4">
    <aside class="col-lg-3">
        @Html.Partial("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureTopics.cshtml")
    </aside>
    <section class="col-lg-9">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Work Items in the Basic Process

There are 3 work items in Azure Boards with the Basic process:

    •   Epic: Under epic, we can create multiple types of issues.

    •   Issue: Issue may be a bug, user story, or an improvement.

    •   Task: Task is the smallest unit of work, for each issue we can create multiple tasks.

In this article, we will look into the process of creating a project on Azure DevOps using Basic Process.</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

            @await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLessonNavigation.cshtml")
</section>
</div>
<style>
.azure-notes-text{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:normal;font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;background:#fff;border:0;padding:0;margin:0;color:#212529;}
